1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
You don't need to hire a firm to

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,813
red-team your strategy.

3
00:00:04,813 --> 00:00:07,000
You can build it in-house.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,964
One: give it a charter.

5
00:00:08,964 --> 00:00:12,107
The red team's job isn't to be negative

6
00:00:12,107 --> 00:00:15,250
— it's to make every big plan survive

7
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:18,000
a serious, structured attack before you commit.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,920
Two: protect its independence.

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,760
A red team that reports to the person

10
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:27,600
who owns the plan will pull its punches.

11
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:30,000
Independence is the entire point.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,743
Three: give it a cadence and a method.

13
00:00:32,743 --> 00:00:35,486
Run a key assumptions check and a premortem

14
00:00:35,486 --> 00:00:38,229
on every major bet — same rhythm, every

15
00:00:38,229 --> 00:00:38,571
quarter.

16
00:00:38,571 --> 00:00:41,314
That's what turns it from a stunt into

17
00:00:41,314 --> 00:00:42,000
a capability.

18
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
If you started one next quarter, which decision

19
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
would you point it at first?
